# Access via `router.query`

```jsx
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';

const router = useRouter();
const { id } = router.query;
```

* `router.query` is an object containing all dynamic segments.
* During pre‑rendering, `router.query` is empty; use `getStaticProps` or `getServerSideProps` to access params on the server.
* For client‑side navigation, it's available immediately after mount.

slides.codeSnippet:
// pages/posts/[id].js
export default function Post({ post }) {
  return <article><h1>{post.title}</h1><p>{post.body}</p></article>;
}

export async function getStaticProps({ params }) {
  const res = await fetch(`https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/${params.id}`);
  const post = await res.json();
  return { props: { post } };
}

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  // define which ids to pre‑render
  return { paths: [{ params: { id: '1' } }, { params: { id: '2' } }], fallback: false };
}
